WEBVTT

00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:14,110
I thought the rife would be noisier, but the new programs of the Atelier Robin

00:00:14,910 --> 00:00:22,430
often have no sound is this normal. Yes, so the difference with the Atelier Robin and the

00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:27,790
true rife at least one difference is with the Atelier Robin you could run the harmonics with it.

00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:34,830
So most of the new, most of the programming that I have created with the Atelier Robin

00:00:35,390 --> 00:00:41,710
is written in harmonics. I wrote all the programs of the Atelier Robin.

00:00:42,430 --> 00:00:50,750
So if it's running a harmonic in the program that you're running, often there'll be no sound whatsoever

00:00:51,950 --> 00:00:57,070
compared to the true rife, which could be loud at different times, especially running a lower

00:00:57,070 --> 00:01:02,590
frequency. The Atelier Robin you could have sound at different times if you're running a lower

00:01:02,590 --> 00:01:07,310
frequency that's not in a harmonic, but typically if you're running a harmonic you're going to have

00:01:07,310 --> 00:01:18,510
very little to no sound. So yes, that is normal.

